Android/bionic: nl_langinfo(CODESET) is __INTRODUCED_IN(26), so at API 24 the
declaration in <langinfo.h> is hidden but the CODESET macro is still defined.
CUPS guards the nl_langinfo call with `#ifdef CODESET`, which is therefore true
even though the function isn't available, causing an implicit-declaration error.

Fix: on Android below API 26, undefine CODESET right after the include so the
nl_langinfo path compiles out. CUPS already falls back to UTF-8 when no charset
is detected, which is the correct default for Android anyway. Minimal, scoped to
__ANDROID_API__ < 26.

--- a/cups/language.c
+++ b/cups/language.c
@@ -17,6 +17,12 @@
 #include "debug-internal.h"
 #ifdef HAVE_LANGINFO_H
 #  include <langinfo.h>
+/* Android/bionic: nl_langinfo() is only available at API >= 26, but CODESET is
+ * defined regardless. Undefine it on older API levels so the nl_langinfo() call
+ * below compiles out and CUPS falls back to its UTF-8 default. */
+#  if defined(__ANDROID__) && defined(__ANDROID_API__) && __ANDROID_API__ < 26
+#    undef CODESET
+#  endif
 #endif /* HAVE_LANGINFO_H */
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #  include <io.h>
